# === Punt Labs canonical .gitignore ===
# Source of truth: .bin/gitignore-canonical.template
# Rollout:         .bin/gitignore-canonical-rollout.sh
# Repo-specific additions belong BELOW the "# === Repo-specific ===" marker.
# Everything above it is managed by the rollout script.

# --- Secrets & local overrides ---
.env
.env.*
.env*.local
!.env.example
.envrc.local
.biff.local
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.*
.claude/mcp.local.json
.mcp.local.json
*.local
*.local.*
.*.local
.*.local.*

# --- Punt Labs runtime state (never commit) ---
.punt-labs/local/
.punt-labs/**/local/**
.punt-labs/**/*.local.*
.punt-labs/quarry/captures/
.punt-labs/vox/ephemeral/
.punt-labs/vox/vox.local.md
.punt-labs/lux.md

# --- Claude Code runtime state ---
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
.claude/scheduled_tasks*
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/projects/
.claude/beadle.poll.*
*/**/.claude/

# --- Lock files (except uv.lock) ---
.*.lock
*.punt-import.lock
.CLAUDE.md.lock
.CLAUDE.md.punt-import.lock
**/.create.lock

# --- Beads runtime state ---
.beads/bd.sock*
.beads/beads.db*
.beads/daemon-*
.beads/daemon.log
.beads/daemon-error
.beads/.local_version

# --- Scratch / temp ---
.tmp/*
!.tmp/.gitkeep
*.tmp
CLAUDE.md.tmp

# --- Worktrees ---
.worktrees/

# --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db

# --- Editors / IDEs ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/
.codex/
.accio/
.claude-flow/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.mypy_cache/
.pyright/
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-work/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
uv.toml

# --- Node / web ---
node_modules/
.astro/
.vercel/

# --- Go ---
coverage.out
*.test

# --- Swift / Xcode ---
# (Do NOT ignore *.xcodeproj / *.xcworkspace — those directories are tracked;
# only ignore user-specific state INSIDE them.)
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
CoverageDerived/
*.xccheckout
*.xcresult
*.xcscmblueprint
*.hmap
*.dSYM
*.dSYM.zip
*.ipa
.swiftpm/
Package.pin
Package.resolved
Carthage/Build/
Carthage/Checkout
Pods/
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
fastlane/test_output
iOSInjectionProject/
playground.xcworkspace
timeline.xctimeline

# --- LaTeX build artifacts ---
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.run.xml
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# === Repo-specific ===
# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.log
*.out
*.run.xml
*.pdf
*.toc
*.synctex.gz

# TTS ephemeral audio
.tts/

# Session transcripts
*-transcript.txt

# Go build artifacts. `/beadle-daemon` was tracked by accident and, at 9.7 MB,
# was 98% of the repo's root-level payload — which matters more after the
# plugin/ move than before it: a git-subdir install is a cone-mode sparse
# checkout, and cone mode always materializes the files sitting in the repo
# root even when it excludes every directory but plugin/. Rebuild it with
# `make build-daemon`.
/beadle-email
/beadle-daemon
dist/
coverage.out

# MCP (project-local, not part of plugin distribution)
.mcp.json
docs/fuzz.sty
docs/*.mf
docs/*.pk
docs/*.tfm
docs/*.aux
docs/*.log
docs/*.fuzz
docs/*.toc

# Ethos per-session and per-mission local state. Machine-local by
# construction — one file per session id, written live by the running
# session's own writer. Tracking it races every git operation that needs a
# clean tree: the v0.16.2 release preflight and its post-merge checkout both
# failed on an audit file being appended to while the release ran. The
# `.punt-labs/` half of this (`.punt-labs/local/`, `.punt-labs/quarry/
# captures/`) now lives in the canonical block above; `.ethos/` is the
# repo-root mission log, which is the same live-writer hazard and, being
# tracked, also shipped 37 internal mission records — handles, tickets, and
# team email addresses — to every plugin user.
.ethos/

# The mandated sibling lock every punt CLI takes before mutating a shared
# host file (tool-enable-disable.md 2.4). Per-machine runtime state, and it
# persists by design — unlinking a lock file races the next writer. The
# pattern is broad because the lock's name is the host file's, and tools
# differ on the suffix — .CLAUDE.md.lock and .CLAUDE.md.punt-import.lock
# both appear.
.*.lock

# Beadle-efv v0.16.3 payload trim: internal materials that used to be tracked
# and therefore were believed to ship to every marketplace-plugin user's
# cache. Re-evaluated and reverted for .envrc 2026-08-23 (see below), and for
# prfaq.tex/prfaq.pdf/prfaq.bib on the same theory below. research/ and
# meetings/ remain excluded pending their own re-evaluation.
#
# .envrc was excluded here from PR #238 through 2026-08-23 on the theory that
# cone-mode sparse-checkout only excludes whole *directories* and therefore
# materializes every root-level file regardless of the git-subdir
# "path": "plugin" scoping. That theory is disproven: a direct inspection of
# `~/.claude/plugins/cache/punt-labs/<plugin>/<version>/` for every
# punt-labs git-subdir plugin, including a fresh beadle v0.16.4 install via
# beadle/install.sh, shows the installed cache contains ONLY the `path`
# directory's contents (plugin/hooks, plugin/commands, plugin/.claude-plugin)
# -- no .git, no .envrc, no root-level files of any kind reach a consumer's
# disk. ARCHITECTURE.md's "Repository Layout" claim about cone mode is
# corrected accordingly. .envrc is tracked again, matching dungeon, ethos,
# mcp-proxy, prfaq, punt-kit, quarry, vox, biff, lux, z-spec, and
# public-website. prfaq.tex/prfaq.pdf/prfaq.bib are tracked again for the
# same reason: they are root-level files under the same disproven theory.
# prfaq.pdf additionally needs a negation here: the broader `*.pdf` LaTeX
# build-artifact rule above (line 169) still matches it, so removing only
# the specific prfaq.pdf line above left it re-ignored for anyone who
# doesn't already have it tracked (caught by Bugbot on PR #246).
research/
meetings/
!prfaq.pdf

# `.punt-labs/ethos/` was excluded here on the theory that its ~1 MB / 245
# files of org-wide identities, roles, personalities, and writing styles get
# cloned into every plugin user's cache. That is the same payload-leak theory
# the .envrc correction above disproves, for the identical reason: cone-mode
# git-subdir only ever materializes the `path: "plugin"` directory's
# contents, and `.punt-labs/` is not under `plugin/`. Per org policy
# (punt-labs/CLAUDE.md "Team Registry"), every repo tracks an inline vendored
# copy at `.punt-labs/ethos/` — plain committed files, never a git submodule
# (a submodule's gitlink IS fetched by a `--recurse-submodules` clone, unlike
# plain tracked files, which is the one real leak vector the no-submodule
# policy guards against — no ignore rule is needed for it, since nothing
# here ever adds a submodule in the first place).

# Vendored ethos runtime state (regenerated per-machine — vendored registry
# only). Matches lux's .gitignore pattern for the same inline-vendored setup.
.punt-labs/ethos/missions/
.punt-labs/ethos/missions.jsonl
.punt-labs/ethos/sessions/
.punt-labs/ethos/.biff
